WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
A movie theater in your
town cuts its ticket

2
00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:04.130
price for one week.

3
00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:05.500
Nothing else is different.

4
00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:08.670
Same movies, same seats, same popcorn.

5
00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.580
But now the line stretches
around the block,

6
00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.830
and far more tickets get sold.

7
00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:17.090
The owner tells everyone
that demand is way up.

8
00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:20.270
An economist would say: not so fast.

9
00:00:20.270 --> 00:00:23.060
So why do economists
insist that a price cut

10
00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:25.200
does not increase demand?

11
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.810
In this mission, you'll
draw demand curves and learn

12
00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.000
the key determinants of demand.

13
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.120
Then you'll use the
graph lab to predict what

14
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:35.600
happens to the curve when
one thing changes at a time.

15
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.370
Your mission: find out exactly
what a price cut changes,

16
00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:40.910
and what it leaves alone.
